      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am trying to make sure that if user intent to have reviewer so system doesn\u0027t change this because it auto-add it as cc.\n\n\nhere is AI answer:\n\nThe heuristic relies on distinguishing between an explicit user request and an implicit system action:\n\nExplicit requests: When a user explicitly sets someone to CC (e.g. via REST API POST /changes/{id}/reviewers with state: CC), allowDowngradeToCC is true (default), allowing deliberate demotion from REVIEWER to CC.\nImplicit system actions: Auto-adding the author/committer as CC upon pushing a patch set (via newReviewerInputFromCommitIdentity) is an implicit system side-effect of git push. An implicit system action should not override an explicit prior user action that designated the account as a REVIEWER.\nThe same design rationale already applies to implicit group CC expansions (where keepExistingReviewers prevents demoting existing reviewers when a group is added as CC).\n\nI have added inline documentation in ReviewerModifier.java to make this distinction explicit for future maintainers.",
